From: Manuel de Brito Fontes <aledbf@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:30:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] bpf: Parse vmlinux BTF in the background during boot

vmlinux BTF is parsed lazily, by the first caller of
bpf_get_btf_vmlinux(). During boot that is an initcall on the boot CPU:
inet_init, through xfrm_init and register_xfrm_state_bpf(), and the
parse is all of its time - 11.2 of inet_init's 11.8 ms under
function_graph, nested under KVM on an AWS c8i.4xlarge.

Start the parse from a core_initcall with async_schedule(), once the
secondary CPUs are up, so it runs beside the subsys and fs initcalls
instead of inside one. Its first caller still takes btf_vmlinux_lock
and waits for whatever of the parse is left.

Local patch for this machine. Not upstream.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 kernel/bpf/verifier.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

--- a/kernel/bpf/verifier.c
+++ b/kernel/bpf/verifier.c
@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@
 #include <net/xdp.h>
 #include <linux/trace_events.h>
 #include <linux/kallsyms.h>
+#include <linux/async.h>
 
 #include "diagnostics.h"
 #include "disasm.h"
@@ -20712,6 +20713,26 @@
 }
 
 /*
+ * Parse vmlinux BTF in the background as soon as the secondary CPUs are up,
+ * rather than on the boot CPU inside whichever initcall first asks for it
+ * (inet_init, through register_xfrm_state_bpf()). The first caller of
+ * bpf_get_btf_vmlinux() still takes btf_vmlinux_lock and so waits for the
+ * parse if it is not done yet; nothing changes for it but when.
+ */
+static void __init btf_vmlinux_parse_async(void *data, async_cookie_t cookie)
+{
+	bpf_get_btf_vmlinux();
+}
+
+static int __init btf_vmlinux_parse_early(void)
+{
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF))
+		async_schedule(btf_vmlinux_parse_async, NULL);
+	return 0;
+}
+core_initcall(btf_vmlinux_parse_early);
+
+/*
  * The add_fd_from_fd_array() is executed only if fd_array_cnt is non-zero. In
  * this case expect that every file descriptor in the array is either a map or
  * a BTF. Everything else is considered to be trash.
-- 
